// The live accounts, in the order they opened. Rendered as inline SVG rather
// than <img> so the glyphs inherit `currentColor` and can be tinted on hover;
// three raster logos could not.
//
// Every mark is reduced to a single-colour glyph, which is a deliberate
// modification of the supplied source art, not laziness:
//   - Instagram ships as a gradient badge. The path here is the *white cutout*
//     lifted verbatim out of the 2022 logo — the camera outline alone, with the
//     squircle and its gradient dropped. Instagram's guidelines permit the
//     one-colour glyph; the gradient would be the only place on this site where
//     colour arrives from outside the magenta→volt ramp.
//   - LinkedIn ships as a rounded square with the "in" knocked out. The
//     container is dropped and only the "in" kept, because the brief bans
//     rounded corners and that bug would otherwise own the only ones here.
//   - GitHub is the Octicons mark unchanged apart from its fill; it was already
//     a bare monochrome glyph.
//
// The viewBoxes differ per glyph and are each cropped to that glyph's own
// bounds, so a single box size below renders all three at a matched optical
// size instead of at whatever padding the source art happened to carry.
